      "pluginVersion": "13.1.3",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "quantile(0.1, DCGM_FI_DEV_POWER_USAGE / DCGM_FI_DEV_ENFORCED_POWER_LIMIT)",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "p10",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "quantile(0.5, DCGM_FI_DEV_POWER_USAGE / DCGM_FI_DEV_ENFORCED_POWER_LIMIT)",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "quantile(0.9, DCGM_FI_DEV_POWER_USAGE / DCGM_FI_DEV_ENFORCED_POWER_LIMIT)",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "p90",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Power / TDP distribution across GPUs",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Layer 4 per node. Two nodes running the same model should look alike; one that does not is either running a different precision, falling back to non-tensor kernels, or throttled. Cross-check a low node against DCGM_FI_DEV_CLOCKS_EVENT_REASONS on Node Health before blaming the code - a thermally-braked GPU produces exactly this shape.\n\nRequires the DCGM_FI_PROF_* profiling fields in monitoring/exporters/dcgm-counters.csv (Volta or newer; conflicts with a concurrent Nsight/profiler session). Empty without them.",
