      "description": "Energy consumed by the fleet's GPUs, per hour.\n\nDCGM_FI_DEV_TOTAL_ENERGY_CONSUMPTION is a monotonic counter in MILLIJOULES since driver load (see monitoring/exporters/dcgm-counters.csv). 1 kWh = 3.6e6 J = 3.6e9 mJ, so the hourly increase is divided by 3.6e9 to give kWh. Read it against SM active above: the same kWh buying half the warp activity is the cost of hollow running, in the unit the facility is billed in.",
